Dear Dr. Raman,

Thank you for RFQ KVP-RFQ-26-0311 and KVP-SPC-2408 Rev X1. Our DFM review aga=
inst LPC-QM-021 Rev C and LPC-LL-003 is complete; 10 items need your decision=
 (3 high risk):

 1. [R-03] Core pitch =C2=B1 0.3 =C2=B5m on 24 channels (risk: Medium)
    Your requirement: 127.0 =C2=B1 0.3 =C2=B5m adjacent pitch, 24 ch
    LPC capability  : Standard substrates =C2=B1 0.5 =C2=B5m; =C2=B1 0.3 =C2=
=B5m needs grade A substrates (LPC-QM-021 =C2=A74.1, =C2=A711.1). A grade A 2=
4-ch design does not exist; new design + grade A qualification.
    LPC proposal    : 127.0 =C2=B1 0.5 =C2=B5m with a new 24-groove grade STD=
 substrate (LPC-DWG-SUB-2412).
    Impact          : Grade A 24-ch would add approx. USD 9 per pc and 3 week=
s.

 2. [R-04] Cumulative pitch =E2=89=A4 0.6 =C2=B5m over 24 ch (risk: Medium)
    Your requirement: Cumulative error =E2=89=A4 0.6 =C2=B5m; absolute =C2=B1=
 0.8 =C2=B5m
    LPC capability  : Cumulative pitch =E2=89=A4 1.0 =C2=B5m standard, =E2=89=
=A4 0.8 =C2=B5m best (LPC-QM-021 =C2=A74.1). Absolute core position =C2=B1 0.=
8 =C2=B5m standard.
    LPC proposal    : Cumulative =E2=89=A4 0.8 =C2=B5m with incoming groove m=
easurement of each substrate lot; absolute =C2=B1 0.8 =C2=B5m; 100 % core-pos=
ition measurement.
    Impact          : Incoming inspection of 5 substrates per lot.

 3. [R-05] Flatness =E2=89=A4 0.3 =C2=B5m over 5 mm width (risk: Low)
    Your requirement: Polish angle 8.0=C2=B0 =C2=B1 0.2=C2=B0; flatness =E2=
=89=A4 0.3 =C2=B5m
    LPC capability  : Polish angle =C2=B1 0.2=C2=B0 best with 100 % interfero=
metry; flatness =E2=89=A4 1.0 =C2=B5m standard, =E2=89=A4 0.5 =C2=B5m best (L=
PC-QM-021 =C2=A74.2).
    LPC proposal    : 8.0=C2=B0 =C2=B1 0.2=C2=B0 (100 % interferometry); flat=
ness =E2=89=A4 0.5 =C2=B5m. With index-matched attach the flatness has little=
 optical effect (=C2=A711.3).
    Impact          : None in application.

 4. [R-06] MPO-12 elite =E2=89=A4 0.25 dB (risk: High)
    Your requirement: FA =E2=89=A4 0.20 dB; MPO-12 APC elite =E2=89=A4 0.25 dB
    LPC capability  : Fibre array =E2=89=A4 0.30 dB standard, =E2=89=A4 0.20 =
dB best; MPO APC =E2=89=A4 0.35 dB standard, =E2=89=A4 0.25 dB only with elit=
e-grade ferrules (LPC-QM-021 =C2=A74.3). The approved MPO-12 kit (PP-MPO12-AP=
C-F) is standard grade.
    LPC proposal    : FA =E2=89=A4 0.30 dB (=E2=89=A4 0.20 dB typical); MPO-1=
2 standard grade =E2=89=A4 0.35 dB random mate. Elite MPO-12 kits would need =
a new supplier qualification (8 weeks).
    Impact          : Kalvara link budget to use 0.35 dB per MPO-12.

 5. [R-07] RL =E2=89=A5 65 dB at both ends (risk: Low)
    Your requirement: =E2=89=A5 65 dB both ends
    LPC capability  : 8=C2=B0 APC fibre array =E2=89=A5 60 dB standard / =E2=
=89=A5 65 dB best; MPO APC =E2=89=A5 60 dB standard (LPC-QM-021 =C2=A74.3).
    LPC proposal    : =E2=89=A5 60 dB at both ends (array end face index-matc=
hed in use).
    Impact          : None in application.

 6. [R-02] Borosilicate lid on fused-silica substrate (risk: Medium)
    Your requirement: Borosilicate lid (lowest cost)
    LPC capability  : Lid and substrate of different glass fail extended ther=
mal cycling (CTE mismatch, LPC-LL-003 LL-01 / DR-01); R-09 asks for 1000 cycl=
es.
    LPC proposal    : Fused-silica lid 5.0 x 5.0 x 0.7 mm (same glass as the =
substrate).
    Impact          : Lid approx. + USD 1.4 per pc.

 7. [R-08] Underfill cure 150 =C2=B0C / 2 h after attach (risk: High)
    Your requirement: FAU survives 150 =C2=B0C / 2 h
    LPC capability  : Cured arrays: 125 =C2=B0C continuous, 150 =C2=B0C for 1=
 h (LPC-QM-021 =C2=A74.5, =C2=A711.5).
    LPC proposal    : Underfill cure =E2=89=A4 125 =C2=B0C (e.g. 125 =C2=B0C =
/ 3 h) or =E2=89=A4 150 =C2=B0C for =E2=89=A4 1 h.
    Impact          : Kalvara cure profile change.

 8. [R-09] 1000 thermal cycles on every lot (risk: Medium)
    Your requirement: DH 1000 h + TC 1000 cycles on every production lot
    LPC capability  : Lot qualification 1000 h damp heat + 500 cycles; 1000 c=
ycles in-house possible (LPC-QM-021 =C2=A76, =C2=A711.9).
    LPC proposal    : 1000 cycles once as design qualification (in-house, NRE=
); every lot 1000 h damp heat + 500 cycles, 11 pcs each, =CE=94IL =E2=89=A4 0=
.2 dB.
    Impact          : Lot release not blocked by 1000-cycle tests.

 9. [R-10] Ink marking on the substrate (risk: Medium)
    Your requirement: Serial number ink-printed on the substrate side face
    LPC capability  : Marking on glass parts not used - laser marking prohibi=
ted, ink and engraving contaminate the end face and bond area (LPC-QM-021 =C2=
=A75, =C2=A711.8).
    LPC proposal    : Polyimide flag label on the sleeve 50 mm behind the boo=
t (P/N, serial, rev); serial also in the IL / RL data file.
    Impact          : No cost impact.

10. [R-15] Samples in 4 weeks / 2,000 pcs by 2026-10-16 (risk: High)
    Your requirement: 100 samples in 4 weeks; 2,000 pcs by 2026-10-16
    LPC capability  : New substrate design 5 weeks; first samples 3-4 weeks a=
fter substrates (LPC-QM-021 =C2=A710).
    LPC proposal    : 100 samples at Kalvara 2026-09-18; 400 pcs 2026-10-02; =
750 pcs 2026-10-16; 750 pcs 2026-10-30.
    Impact          : Samples 3 weeks and last 750 pcs 2 weeks later than req=
uested.

Based on production experience (LPC-LL-003): item 6 (LL-01, DR-01).
Delivery plan: Samples 100 pcs at Kalvara 2026-09-18; Lot 1 400 pcs at Kalvar=
a 2026-10-02; Lot 2 750 pcs at Kalvara 2026-10-16; Lot 3 750 pcs at Kalvara 2=
026-10-30.
Unit price expected above your target of USD 105.00; NRE quoted separately.
Please confirm by 2026-07-09.

Best regards,
